4
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:10,870
In particular, when it comes to ads

5
00:00:10,870 --> 00:00:12,190
that seem like they should work,

6
00:00:12,290 --> 00:00:13,850
but they're just not for some reason.

7
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:16,870
So to start, we're going to start with a question

8
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:18,750
that I get all the time, which is,

9
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:20,370
Sarah, this ad should be working.

10
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:21,470
Why is it not?

11
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:22,550
Why is it not?

12
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:24,470
And it's always interesting when I get this question

13
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:25,890
because it's always about a product

14
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:27,150
or an ad in particular

15
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:29,430
that has a good offer included in it.

16
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:30,470
It's got a strong headline.

17
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:31,530
It's beautiful, creative.

18
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:33,310
It's well-developed, well-designed,

19
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:35,070
but it's still not converting.

20
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:36,470
And it's really interesting

21
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,050
because it's kind of a gut punch moment

22
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:40,150
when you're sitting here saying,

23
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:41,390
I have done all this research.

24
00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:43,370
I know this should hit with our audience.

25
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:45,650
Why is this not working, right?

26
00:00:45,970 --> 00:00:46,910
Why does this happen?

27
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:49,630
So typically when I see brands do this,

28
00:00:49,690 --> 00:00:52,270
most of the time when they run into an ad

29
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:53,590
that should have worked but didn't,

30
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:55,290
they want to shift all kinds of things.

31
00:00:55,370 --> 00:00:57,290
They want to change targeting or make it a GIF

32
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:59,570
or get a new UGC creator on board

33
